From: Niklas Sheth <niklassheth@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dracut: include gravity-firmware in hostonly builds off-device

Commit 084cbae made check() return 1 when dracut runs hostonly without
/proc/device-tree/chosen/gravity,efi-system-partition. dracut.conf.d forces
the module with add_dracutmodules, so every hostonly initramfs built off the
device (kiwi image builds, chroots, a boot whose stage1 did not forward the
ESP) fails with "Module 'gravity-firmware' cannot be installed" and
kernel-install aborts. Restore asahi-scripts' behaviour: include it.

--- a/dracut/modules.d/99gravity-firmware/module-setup.sh
+++ b/dracut/modules.d/99gravity-firmware/module-setup.sh
@@ -5,9 +5,9 @@
 check() {
     if [ -n "$hostonly" ] &&
        [ ! -e /proc/device-tree/chosen/gravity,efi-system-partition ]; then
-       return 1
+       return 0
     elif [ -z "$hostonly" ]; then
         return 0
     else
        return 0
     fi
